        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Fix incorrect Chinese calendar example in Temporal.PlainDate.from docs]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42660</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42660"/>
        <updated>2026-01-07T14:19:54.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44868357?u=096bd31a657e3fc94f4821b3b53e251c7c1d07f6&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Updates the Chinese calendar example in <code class="notranslate">Temporal.PlainDate.from()</code> documentation:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Corrects the comment about epoch year alignment (Chinese year 2021 = ISO year 2021)</li>
<li>Fixes expected output: <code class="notranslate">"2021-08-08[u-ca=chinese]"</code> instead of <code class="notranslate">"-000616-08-12[u-ca=chinese]"</code></li>
<li>Adds Hebrew calendar example showing significant epoch year difference (5781 Hebrew = 2021 ISO)</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Per <a href="https://tc39.es/proposal-intl-era-monthcode/#table-epoch-years" rel="nofollow">TC39 proposal</a>, the Chinese calendar's epoch is ISO year 0, not -616 BCE.</p>
